{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. You're here today for a scheduled bronchoscopy to help with your tracheal stenosis. How are you feeling this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’m okay, a bit nervous. My breathing’s been a little tight lately, but not worse than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your history of relapsing polychondritis has caused narrowing in your airway, and we’re going to do a balloon dilation today to open it up a bit. It’s a routine procedure for you, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had it a few times before. Last time was in February. It helped for a while, but it’s starting to close up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll use a balloon to stretch the narrowed areas in your trachea and possibly the left main bronchus. We’ll also take some biopsies and washings to check for any changes or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Biopsies? Is something new going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of anything serious, but it’s standard to check. We want to make sure the inflammation isn’t getting worse and rule out infection. You’ve been on tobramycin — that’s to prevent lung infections, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I inhale it twice a day. My pulmonologist said it helps keep the bacteria down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll continue that. Now, your labs this morning show a high white blood cell count — 23.8. But given your condition, that’s likely from inflammation, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:14:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s been high before. My rheumatologist says it’s from the polychondritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll keep an eye on it. You’ll stay overnight for observation after the procedure, just to make sure your breathing stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:17:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I’d rather be safe. Any pain expected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You might have some mild soreness or discomfort in your airway. We’ll give you lidocaine nebulizers and pain meds like Tylenol or tramadol if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:20:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my oxygen? I’m on 40% through the trach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-03-16 06:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on the 40% trach mask today and monitor your saturation. It’s been in the mid-90s, which is acceptable. We’ll do a chest X-ray after the procedure too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-03-16 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You just came back from the bronchoscopy. Everything went smoothly — they dilated multiple areas in your airway and took biopsies. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-03-16 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired. My throat feels raw, and I can taste a little blood. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-03-16 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s expected. The scope and balloon can irritate the airway. We’ll keep you on the trach mask and give you lidocaine nebs to numb it. No fever or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-03-16 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just the soreness. Breathing feels a bit easier already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-03-16 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. We’ll watch you closely tonight. Your chest X-ray shows the trach tube is in place, and no new issues in the lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-03-16 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, can I drink water yet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-03-16 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet — we need to wait a few more hours to make sure your throat is healing and you can swallow safely. We’ll reassess in a couple of hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-03-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Vital signs are stable, oxygen is 95% on 40% trach. You can try small sips of water now — slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-03-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll take it slow. Any news on the washings they took?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-03-16 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Preliminary report shows Serratia marcescens and Proteus mirabilis, but in low amounts. They’re considered part of your normal respiratory flora right now, not an active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-03-16 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? I’ve heard of Serratia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-03-16 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but in your case, it’s likely just colonizing your airway due to your trach and chronic lung changes. We’ll continue your inhaled tobramycin to keep it in check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-03-16 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling better. Can I go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-03-16 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you stay stable. We’re keeping you overnight to make sure there’s no bleeding or swelling that could block your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your repeat chest X-ray looks stable — trach tube in place, no pneumonia. Your oxygen is 93% on 40%, and you’re eating and drinking fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. So I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you today. We’re giving you a steroid taper — prednisone — to reduce airway inflammation after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like last time? I remember that helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, starting at 40 mg and tapering down over five days. Also, keep taking your regular meds — losartan, famotidine, calcium, and the inhaled tobramycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Interventional pulmonology will contact you to schedule your next bronchoscopy in about four weeks. They’ll review the biopsy results then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start having trouble breathing or cough up more blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Come back right away. Also, call your pulmonologist if you have fever, increased mucus, or worsening pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch for that. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-03-17 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon. Rest well at home, and keep that follow-up appointment."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-03-16 00:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-03-17 16:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for observation following a scheduled flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of multi-level airway stenosis due to relapsing polychondritis and Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome. The procedure was completed without complications, and he remained hemodynamically stable throughout the admission, with oxygen saturations in the mid- to high-90s on 40% trach mask. Mild post-procedural pain was managed with analgesics. Bronchial washings showed Serratia marcescens and Proteus mirabilis, interpreted as colonizing flora rather than active infection. Biopsies were obtained and pending at discharge. A prednisone taper was prescribed to reduce inflammation, and he was discharged home with follow-up planned with interventional pulmonology in four weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Tracheal stenosis",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Chronic respiratory failure, unspecified whether with hypoxia or hypercapnia",
      "Pulmonary fibrosis, unspecified",
      "Other diseases of bronchus, not elsewhere classified",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Atrophy of testis",
      "Long term (current) use of antibiotics",
      "Carrier of other infectious diseases"
    ]
  }
}
